# Force LF regardless of the contributor's core.autocrlf.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, and two things here care: the
# .mjs deploy scripts, and the .sql migrations, which are read and hashed by
# `wrangler d1 migrations apply` - a CRLF migration is a different file from the
# one already recorded as applied.
*.mjs       text eol=lf
*.ts        text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.jsonc     text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to "fix" them.
*.png       binary
